Redirects are server-controlled input (CA-CAKE-03): follow at most 10, stay on
http/https, never downgrade https to http, and off the listed host only to a
public address. The upload endpoint reached after redirects is reported as
"resolved_upload_url" so the caller can see where the transfer really went.

The TCP control connection (CA-CAKE-05) reads lines through a 4 KiB buffer
instead of growing without bound, and every command gets a deadline so a
server that stops answering cannot hold the sampler forever.

